        {
          "name": "circular-route-blank-en-found-by-chinese-name",
          "why": "NAMED BOUNDARY ROW (empty `en` on a circular route). The GMB circular terminus whose English name upstream is an empty string. Two things must hold at once: the Chinese query finds it, AND the active locale is `en` — so the candidate list must fall through the two blank English entries to the Chinese ones. A port that reads only the active locale's name, or that treats a blank name as a reason to skip the stop entirely, makes this stop unsearchable for the majority of HK riders, who type Chinese. That is why the row is not decorative: the blank is in the field the code looks at FIRST.",
